# Exocortex — Master Plan

**Status (2026-08-27, Round 6):** RELEASE BLOCKED. A strict whole-project
review at `f7bf463` reopened 30 blocking findings, eight advisory findings,
and four verification questions. The authoritative ledger and closure
criteria are `docs/reviews/round-6-review.prd`; accepted work is promoted in
the Backlog below as R6-S1 through R6-Q1. The prior post-BR-PRD green-gate
claim is historical, not the current release verdict.

**Status (2026-08-27):** Palantir-expansion PRD drafted
(`docs/exocortex-palantir-expansion-prd.md`, rev 2) — five post-v1
capabilities promoted below as PX1-PX6. **None are release-blocking and
none start while Round 6 is open**; they are recorded here so the plan
reflects accepted scope rather than living only in a PRD. PX1 closes the
long-standing v2 deferral D2 ("second-pack demo"). PX3 is the one item
with a bearing on current work: it found that the existing
`storage-conformance` gate does not do what its name implies (see PX3's
note), which is a live weakness in the gate set Round 6 is being verified
against.

**Status:** BR-PRD shipped. **[2026-08-27]** Memory backup/restore
landed as `exocortex-client 0.2.2`: `--export`/`--import` one-shot
modes over a versioned, fingerprint-stamped file in the WAL's own row
shape — all-or-nothing restore (fingerprint gate fails closed, drafts
revalidated against the one rulebook, ids/batch-ids/states preserved
so `Synced` never re-drains), idempotent by construction. All five
acceptance criteria in `client/tests/backup_restore.rs`; the
idempotent-import test additionally caught a real cache defect
(stale search-arena keys on repeated upserts — StableGraph index
reuse vs first-slot-only blanking) — fixed in the same release with
its own regression test. Also this session: the README was
repositioned (structure-over-prose hook, MCR² explainer, feed paths
named, memory-graph lineage section), generated hero images landed
(README + ontology guide), and `docs/ONTOLOGY_GUIDE.md` (the pack
authoring guide) shipped. Remote moved to
`github.com/memory-graph/exocortex`; install URLs now resolve.

**Status:** SR-PRD shipped. **[2026-08-26, night]** Standalone
read-back (F1-F5) landed as `exocortex-client 0.2.1` (see the Done
table's SR-PRD rows). The zero-setup mode's write→read loop is closed:
in-session read-back (AC1), cross-restart seeding with byte-stable ids
(AC2), edges + Conversation grouping traversable (AC3), honest-empty
fresh installs — the synthetic seed is gone (AC4, F4 folded into the
F3 commit: replacing the boot seed left it dead code), backend mode
unchanged (AC5), all-states WAL seeding (AC6), dangling cross-batch
edges dropped-never-served (AC7). The grouping builders are pinned
byte-identical to the backend commit path by parity test. README gap
note retired.

**Status:** A-PRD shipped. **[2026-08-26, later]** The Agent
Instructions PRD (rev 5, D1-D10 + the §4.5/§4.8/§4.9/§4.10 mechanics)
landed as `exocortex-client 0.2.0` — worklist→code map in the Done
table's A-PRD rows; gates green including the new `gen-playbook` drift
gate (48 kinds / 47 assertable; the generator's authored-only filter is
itself drift protection — the ontology registers 87 kinds including
R-T4 companions the playbook must not teach). **Reopened** by a
deployment-model review: `docs/bug-prd-standalone-readback.md` (SR-PRD)
— the zero-setup mode's writes are durable but invisible to every read
(three defects: no live write-back, no boot seeding, synthetic filler
answering searches instead). F1-F5 ship as 0.2.1; ~~the README flags
the gap until they do~~ (closed same day).

**Status (2026-08-26, earlier):** Round 3 complete. Reopened by a
codebase-wide defect audit (`docs/bug-prd-codebase-audit.md`) — 70
confirmed defects — and **closed the same day** (sweep rounds 4-5; see the
Backlog statuses and the Done table). One intended ontology change landed
with the fix set: the fingerprint moved `d8bcd004…4e8c` →
`e1f7d17b…ddc9b2` because the pack now carries the R-T14 `computed_only`
marker (W6; goldens and AGENTS.md updated in the same change). Five new
seam gates (`storage-conformance`, `write-path-parity`,
`dead-enforcement`, `auth-coverage`, `artifact-equivalence`) now cover the
between-crate surface where every audit defect lived. Three review rounds
closed (`docs/reviews/round-{1,2,3}-review.prd`); every accepted item
carries a test that fails without it.

**Purpose:** The authoritative, phased worklist for this repository. Each
round of review findings gets its own `round-<n>-review.prd`; accepted
items are promoted into this file, tracked to done, and never silently
dropped. Anything not listed here is either shipped or explicitly deferred
to v2 in the PRD's own terms.

**Historical baseline (2026-08-27, post-BR-PRD):** 229 tests / 0 failed
across 73 suites (`cargo test --workspace --features
exocortex-adapter-sdk/testing --no-fail-fast` — the feature is
mandatory: a lib canary fails any run that would leave the SDK's
mock-driven suites dark). The known 500ms SSE-window flake
(`sync.rs::sse_feed_observed_by_client_cache_within_500ms` and
`e2e_chain`'s same-class window) remains: pre-existing, green on clean
runs, noisier under heavy parallel builds — observed pass rate varies
with machine load. Full gate pipeline green: fmt, clippy, deny, tests,
kernel-purity, fingerprint (`e1f7d17b…ddc9b2`, unchanged through
SR-PRD and BR-PRD), gen-schemas (7 operations), gen-playbook (48 kinds
/ 47 assertable), no-llm, proto-sync, signing-hygiene, wire-standalone,
plus the five seam gates. `exocortex-client` at 0.2.2; the other 13
crates at 0.1.0.

**Prior baseline (2026-08-26, post-SR-PRD):** 223 tests / 1 flaky
across 72 suites; fingerprint `e1f7d17b…ddc9b2`; `exocortex-client`
at 0.2.1.

**Prior baseline (2026-08-26, post-A-PRD):** 213 tests / 1 flaky
across 71 suites. Full gate pipeline green as above; fingerprint
`e1f7d17b…ddc9b2`; `exocortex-client` at 0.2.0.

**Post-audit baseline (2026-08-26, pre-A-PRD):** 194 tests / 0 failed
across 70 suites; fingerprint `e1f7d17b…ddc9b2`; SLO benches green
(search p50 ≈27µs; khop p50 ≈288µs against the 300µs budget); live
Falkor suites 7/7 (storage), 6/6 (cypher), 3/3 (fencing), 6/6
(cluster), SSE 1/1, cross-node 2/2; 3-node compose converges after
leader-kill in 1290-1448ms (M5 AC < 2s).

**Pre-audit baseline (2026-08-25, post-round-3):** 138 tests / 0 failed
across 68 suites; fingerprint `d8bcd004…4e8c`.

## Initial build (M0–M8, shipped 2026-08)

All nine milestones landed in order, one commit each, every gate green at
each step (88 tests at completion).

| Milestone | Delivered |
|---|---|
| M0 | Workspace scaffolding: kernel, wire, xtask; toolchain/dep pins resolved (deviations recorded in `docs/MILESTONE_REPORT.md`) |
| M1 | Ontology: `pack!` macro engine, dev-v1 pack (13 memory types, 12 entity types, 48 kinds), R-Pk/R-T validators |
| M2 | Storage: `Storage` trait, registered Cypher catalogue, FalkorDB adapter, InMemory double, bi-temporal reads |
| M3 | Cache + MCP client: ArcSwap snapshots, 2Q admission, sled WAL, stdio MCP server, search SLO bench (100k) |
| M4 | Reasoning: Crepe R1–R9 + D1–D6 fixpoints, Steel explain traces + R6, idempotent derived-edge writeback |
| M5 | Cluster: owner leases with epoch fencing, HMAC-signed envelopes, peer admission, SSE change feed |
| M6 | Ingestion: IngestService pipeline (HMAC → checksum → fingerprint → ceiling → triples), entity extraction, `end_session` tool, worker host |
| M7 | Operation registry: one entry per operation, MCP+HTTP schema parity, audit ledger, goldens |
| M8 | Dreams: MCR² + sparsity guardrails, consolidation cycle with rollback, trigger model, discovery proposals |

