| D13 | **2** | **Deterministic entity resolution** — resolve the same real-world entity across producers by shared external identity (`ExternalKey`, typed entities as convergent join points), not by fuzzy matching. Explicitly NOT the ML half: no corpus, no labelled set, no model. Without this the graph is a collection of documents rather than a model of a world, which is the core ontology claim. Fuzzy/probabilistic ER is a separate later item, and `NearDuplicateApplicant` stays a Dreams-computed proposal in the meantime | palantir-expansion PRD §5; core PRD §24 |
